        {
          "id": "commentary_09_1-guidance-1",
          "type": "commentary_guidance",
          "text": "This is an Extended Response question. Please read the information in the introduction to \nthis commentary document regarding how to annotate students' responses.",
          "order": 2,
          "parent_id": null,
          "annotations": [],
          "source": {
            "file": "B-JUN24-84612H-09_1-C.txt",
            "page": null
          },
          "marks": null,
          "level": null,
          "mark_range": null,
          "assessment_objective": null,
          "specification_reference": null
        },
        {
          "id": "commentary_09_1-guidance-2",
          "type": "commentary_guidance",
          "text": "You may find it helpful to download the infographic (star-chart) from the additional supporting \ninformation in OLS. This shows what details are required to gain access (i.e. achieve the \nlower mark) for each Level in a visual format.",
          "order": 3,
          "parent_id": null,
          "annotations": [
            {
              "type": "qualifier",
              "text": "required",
              "start": 145,
              "end": 153
            },
            {
              "type": "qualifier",
              "text": "lower mark",
              "start": 188,
              "end": 198
            }
          ],
          "source": {
            "file": "B-JUN24-84612H-09_1-C.txt",
            "page": null
          },
          "marks": null,
          "level": null,
          "mark_range": null,
          "assessment_objective": null,
          "specification_reference": null
        },
        {
          "id": "commentary_09_1-guidance-3",
          "type": "commentary_guidance",
          "text": "Most of the points in the mark scheme are structured in terms of linked ideas. These are \nrepresented by ‘black bullet points’ and ‘white bullet points’ So to get credit for linked ideas, \nas described in the Generic Level Descriptors at the top of the mark scheme, students must \ngive a black bullet point along with one of its associated white bullet points.",
          "order": 4,
          "parent_id": null,
          "annotations": [
            {
              "type": "qualifier",
              "text": "must",
              "start": 275,
              "end": 279
            },
            {
              "type": "quantifier",
              "text": "one",
              "start": 318,
              "end": 321
            }
          ],
          "source": {
            "file": "B-JUN24-84612H-09_1-C.txt",
            "page": null
          },
          "marks": null,
          "level": null,
          "mark_range": null,
          "assessment_objective": null,
          "specification_reference": null
        },
        {
          "id": "commentary_09_1-guidance-4",
          "type": "commentary_guidance",
          "text": "Beware of bp2 in the indicative content. Credit should only be given if the student refers to \nreduced competition for some factor specified, not just ‘resources’ or ‘nutrients’ which are too \nvague.",
          "order": 5,
          "parent_id": null,
          "annotations": [
            {
              "type": "qualifier",
              "text": "only",
              "start": 55,
              "end": 59
            },
            {
              "type": "domain_term",
              "text": "reduced competition",
              "start": 95,
              "end": 114
            },
            {
              "type": "domain_term",
              "text": "factor",
              "start": 124,
              "end": 130
            },
            {
              "type": "qualifier",
              "text": "not just",
              "start": 142,
              "end": 150
            },
            {
              "type": "domain_term",
              "text": "resources",
              "start": 152,
              "end": 161
            },
            {
              "type": "domain_term",
              "text": "nutrients",
              "start": 167,
              "end": 176
            },
            {
              "type": "qualifier",
              "text": "too",
              "start": 188,
              "end": 191
            },
            {
              "type": "qualifier",
              "text": "vague",
              "start": 193,
              "end": 198
            }
          ],
          "source": {
            "file": "B-JUN24-84612H-09_1-C.txt",
            "page": null
          },
          "marks": null,
          "level": null,
          "mark_range": null,
          "assessment_objective": null,
          "specification_reference": null
        },
        {
          "id": "commentary_09_1-guidance-5",
          "type": "commentary_guidance",
          "text": "Furthermore, many students having referred to bp1, then state words such as ‘…so \nthe GM soya gets more light’ – this is also not sufficient for bp2 as it does not refer to \nreduced competition, well enough, at this level of demand.",
          "order": 6,
          "parent_id": null,
          "annotations": [
            {
              "type": "domain_term",
              "text": "GM soya",
              "start": 86,
              "end": 93
            },
            {
              "type": "domain_term",
              "text": "light",
              "start": 104,
              "end": 109
            },
            {
              "type": "qualifier",
              "text": "not sufficient",
              "start": 126,
              "end": 140
            },
            {
              "type": "domain_term",
              "text": "reduced competition",
              "start": 174,
              "end": 193
            }
          ],
          "source": {
